          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#detection_of_decomposability Detection of decomposability
          #HCohomologyNeverVanishes.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (H-cohomology of weakly
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decomposable+forms"} decomposable forms
                is non-vanishing)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              be a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebra"} graded-commutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \in \mathcal{A}
              be of odd degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(H) = 2 n +1
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is weakly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decomposable+differential+form"} decomposable
              in that it is in the ideal generated by the elements of degree 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi k
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mi i
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi β
                            %mi i
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{k}{\sum}
                    \\underset{deg = 1}{\underbrace{\alpha_i}}
                    \\wedge
                    \\underset{deg = 2n}{\underbrace{\beta_i}}
            %p
              then its H-cohomology (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HCohomologyInGradedCommutativeAlgebra"}
          %p
            This statement and the following proof are due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sackel18"} Sackel 18
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p First consider the following:
            %p
              %em Claim:
              Assuming that the H-cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              did vanish, then for every sequence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi …
                      %mo &lt;
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi ℓ
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i_1 \lt \ldots \lt i_{\ell} \leq k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℓ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_{i_1\cdots i_{\ell}} \in \mathcal{A}
              of degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mn 3
                    %mo −
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(\gamma_{i_1\cdots i_{\ell}}) = k-3-\ell
              (vanishing if
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \gt k-3
              = succeed "-s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %em not
              contained in this sequence
            #eq:ProductsOfAlphas.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi ℓ
                        %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mo =
                              %mi k
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ∧
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi α
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mn 1
                                %mo ^
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ∧
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi α
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi ℓ
                                %mo ^
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ∧
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mi k
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi k
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ∧
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mi k
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha_{\widehat{i_1\cdots i_{\ell}}}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    1 &amp;\vert&amp; \ell = k
                    \\\
                    \\alpha_1
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    \\widehat{\alpha_{i_1}}
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    \\widehat{\alpha_{i_{\ell}}}
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    \\alpha_k
                    \&amp;\vert&amp;
                    1 \lt \ell \lt k
                    \\\
                    \\alpha_1 \wedge \cdots \wedge \alpha_k
                    \&amp;\vert&amp;
                    \\ell =0
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p (hats indicate that the corresponding element is omitted) would satisfy
            #eq:InductiveDecompositionOfAlpha.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi ℓ
                        %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℓ
                        %mo +
                        %mi ℓ
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi H
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi ℓ
                      %mo +
                      %munderover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ℓ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mover
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %mo ^
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi ℓ
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha_{\widehat{i_1\cdots i_{\ell}}}
                    \\;=\;
                    (-1)^{i_1+\cdots+i_{\ell}+\ell}
                    \\left(
                    H
                    \\wedge
                    \\gamma_{i_1\cdots i_{\ell}}
                    +
                    \\sum_{j=1}^{\ell}(-1)^{j+1}
                    \\beta_{i_j}
                    \\wedge
                    \\gamma_{i_1\cdots\widehat{i_j}\cdots i_{\ell}}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that this claim immediately implies the statement
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+by+contradiction"} by contradiction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell = k
              the left hand side of
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InductiveDecompositionOfAlpha"} (2)
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              by definition
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProductsOfAlphas"} (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              are in negative degree. This is a contradiction, implying that the assumption of vanishing H-cohomology must be wrong.
            %p
              Hence it is now sufficient to prove the above claim. We proceed by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
